# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Compiled output of the helper in hack/. Its source sits beside it and the name
# carries no extension, so nothing above catches it — and a `go build` in that
# directory otherwise leaves a multi-megabyte unstripped ELF staged for the next
# `git add .`, which is how one of them reached this branch.
#
# hack/generate_release_notes is the same kind of artefact and is already tracked,
# so listing it here would say nothing: git does not ignore a file it tracks.
# Untracking it is its own change.
/hack/sds-node-configurator-release-notes

# Test binary, build with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Project-local glide cache, RE: https://github.com/Masterminds/glide/issues/736
.glide/

# vim
*.swp

# IDE
.history/
.idea
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
.project
.settings
.idea/
venv/
*.code-workspace
.vscode
*.code-workspace

# macOS Finder files
*.DS_Store
._*

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
/lib/python/dist/

# dev
hack.sh
**/Dockerfile-dev
.secret
images/**/Makefile
local_build.sh
/base_images.yml

# local caches (Cursor/Go/direnv, etc.)
.cache/
.direnv/
.gocache/

images/sds-common-scheduler-extender/REVIEW.md

# test data
test*.log
# e2e local env (keys, hosts) — do not commit to public repo
e2e/config/
e2e/temp/
e2e/.gomodcache/
e2e/.gocache/

# local test artifacts (kubeconfigs, cluster state at repo root)
temp/
.cursor
.tmp*
# git worktrees created by agents
.worktrees/